<title>JAPAN: Sanshin Elec strengthens on firm earnings.</title>
<headline>Sanshin Elec strengthens on firm earnings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sanshin Electronics Co Ltd shares strengthened in the Tuesday morning session, backed by firm earnings which were announced last week, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0137 GMT, the shares of the trader in electronic parts and equipment were up 70 yen at 1,950, a new high for calendar 1997.  </p>
<p>Last week Sanshin said its parent current profit in the year to March 1997 was 6.75 billion yen, up from 3.57 billion yen in the previous year.</p>
